ape  you're good to go and I took them in the  oven at a high temperature for a short  period of time that way your meatballs  have a tender inside can brown all the  way around while you're cooking them the  last step you want to do is clicking  your pasta use a generous pinch of salt  to make sure that your water is salty  briny like the ocean we don't want bland  pasta shimmy it  so it gets Luffy and Goofy you know let  it cook for about seven to ten minutes  until the pasta is al dente now al dente  is this another Italian word that means  to the tooth just undercooked enough  where it has a slight chew but is still  tended the best way to tell that your  pasta is perfectly cooked is just to  taste it yeah see it perfect  when draining your pasta to put it  immediately into your pasta sauce stir  it around so that the wonderfully  simmered sauce covers every single piece  of pasta it's a perfect marriage of  flavors spaghetti and meatballs is just  a classic Italian American dish it's a  recipe that I come back to time and time  again try it at home make it your own  have fun with it and you'll become a  master at spaghetti in no time  [Music]
 

